# GameDrop rules

Authoritative source: [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md). Summary for Cursor:

## Shape of the system

- One invocation = one collection cycle. `cmd/gamedrop/main.go` wires and exits;
  there is no server, API, UI, or in-app scheduler. Never add one.
- Adapters live in `internal/stores/<store>/`, persist through
  `internal/storage` only, and never import `notify`.
- `internal/collector` owns orchestration, concurrency, expiry and notification
  policy. `internal/notify` owns rendering and the outbox processor.
- Deployment: one Fly.io Scheduled Machine + one volume. Never suggest a plain
  `fly deploy`; it would create an always-running Machine.

## Domain rules (do not relax)

- `free_to_keep` requires verified evidence: 100% discount from a non-zero
  original price (Steam `appdetails`, Epic `discountPercentage == 0`, GOG
  `finalMoney == 0 && baseMoney > 0`). Otherwise `unknown` or skip.
- Zero `time.Time` = unknown deadline. Never invent dates.
- Missing from a scan → `missing_since` only; expiry requires a passed `ends_at`.
- Failed or partial source → write nothing; keep previous data.
- Identity is `(store, country, store_offer_id)`; never dedupe by title.
- Notifications are at-least-once via a transactional outbox with dedupe keys.

## Implementation conventions

- Go 1.27, standard library first; only `modernc.org/sqlite` as a dependency.
- Errors wrapped with `%w`; `context.Context` propagated; `slog` with stable keys
  (`run_id`, `source`, `country`, `offer_id`, `duration_ms`, `status`, `error`).
- Never log secrets (bot tokens, chat IDs, cookies) or URLs with query strings.
- Tests: offline, `httptest` + `testdata/` fixtures, `t.TempDir()` databases,
  injected clocks. Add a fixture regression test with every parser fix.
- Commit messages: what changed and why only. Never add attribution or
  `Co-Authored-By` trailers.

## Verify

`gofmt -l .` (empty), `go vet ./...`, `go test ./...`, `go build ./...`. Do not
commit, push, or deploy unless asked.
